Short:        libxmp 4.7.3 link library for AmigaOS 3.x
Author:       Claudio Matsuoka, Hipolito Carraro Jr and libxmp's contributors
Uploader:     AmiCradle Team
Type:         dev/lib
Version:      4.7.3
Requires:     m68k-amigaos-gcc (bebbo's, GCC 6.5 or 16), libnix
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0

libxmp plays MOD, XM, S3M, IT, MED, Oktalyzer, DigiBooster and some 90
module formats. This is libxmp 4.7.3, unchanged, built for AmigaOS 3.x
with libnix (-noixemul), as a static link library. It has every loader,
the depackers (PowerPacker, XPK through xfd-style formats, LhA, ZIP,
gzip, bzip2, xz and more; they unpack to T:) and ProWizard.

  include/xmp.h
  lib/libxmp.a              68040 with an FPU (-m68040 -m68881)
  lib/68000/libxmp.a        any 68k, soft float (-m68000)
  lib/pkgconfig/libxmp.pc   and lib/68000/pkgconfig/libxmp.pc
  examples/xmp-render.c     load a module, mix it to raw PCM
  docs/                     libxmp's README, COPYING, CREDITS, Changelog,
                            the API reference (libxmp.html), the formats,
                            and the notices of the code it bundles

Build with -DLIBXMP_STATIC (the .pc files add it). Link with the same
CPU and FPU flags as the library: a -m68881 program with lib/, any other
with lib/68000/.

  m68k-amigaos-gcc -O2 -m68040 -m68881 -noixemul -DLIBXMP_STATIC \
      -Iinclude examples/xmp-render.c -Llib -lxmp -lm -o xmp-render

Built with GCC 16.2: -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer -mno-bitfield
-fno-delete-null-pointer-checks -fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns, and
checked for GCC 16's misplaced float-to-int store at -m68040 (none).

libxmp is MIT licensed (docs/COPYING); the code it bundles keeps its own
permissive licences (docs/bundled-notices.txt). This build: AmiCradle
Team, https://github.com/DalsinAI/openamigaaudiotools
